# [TARGET: {target_file}] [TASK: {task_id}]

<harness_task id="{task_id}">
  <metadata>
    <agent_role>{agent_role}</agent_role>
    <priority>{priority}</priority>
  </metadata>

  <context_links>
    <!-- Use the Semantic Map (docs/map.md) to locate symbols -->
    <link path="docs/map.md" symbols="{required_symbols}"/>
    <link path="docs/delta/{dependency_id}.json"/>
    
    <!-- Hybrid Reference: Do NOT paste large logs here. Use path references. -->
    {log_references}
  </context_links>

  <reasoning_protocol type="ToT">
    <!-- MANDATORY: You must fill the [THOUGHT_PROCESS] block below before writing code. -->
    <instruction>
      1. [TEST_DESIGN]: Define the behavioral assertions required by the task.
      2. [RED_PHASE]: If this is a *-RED task, describe the specific assertion that will fail and why. DO NOT IMPLEMENT PRODUCTION LOGIC.
      3. [GREEN_PHASE]: If this is a *-GREEN task, describe the implementation logic to satisfy the RED tests.
      4. Predict at least 2 failure modes (Worst-case scenarios).
    </instruction>
    <rationale>TDD prevents "tautological testing" (hallucinated successes) and ensures every line of code is auditable and intentional.</rationale>
  </reasoning_protocol>

  <work_scope>
    <modify path="{target_file}"/>
    <constraints>
      <constraint>Surgical edits only. No refactoring of adjacent code.</constraint>
      <constraint>RED PHASE CONSTRAINT: If task_id ends in "-RED", you are STRICTLY FORBIDDEN from modifying production files. You may only edit files in tests/ or equivalent.</constraint>
      <constraint>Do NOT touch .harness/ or .git/ directories.</constraint>
      <constraint>Do NOT attempt to copy harness.py to the local project directory. Always execute it directly from your skill workspace using its absolute path.</constraint>
      <constraint>DOCUMENTATION CONSTRAINT: During the [DOCUMENT] stage, you are STRICTLY FORBIDDEN from modifying production or test code. You may ONLY update files in the `docs/` directory.</constraint>
    </constraints>
  </work_scope>

  <mechanical_dod>
    <instruction>
      You MUST use the harness CLI to run tests and lock the telemetry hash. 
      
      TDD ENFORCEMENT:
      1. For *-RED tasks, use: `python3 [PATH]/harness.py test --mode tdd-red --id {task_id} --cmd "{cmd}"`
      2. For *-GREEN tasks, use: `python3 [PATH]/harness.py test --id {task_id} --cmd "{cmd}"`
      
      CRITICAL: Standard mode requires MANDATORY Line Coverage >= 80%.
      You MUST use a coverage tool (e.g., `c8`, `nyc`) with your test runner.
      Example: `c8 node --test timer.test.js`
      
      INTEGRITY VIOLATION: The system PHYSICALLY BLOCKS 'grep', 'ls', 'cat', 'echo', and 'node -e' to prevent coverage bypass. 
      Attempting to use these will result in an immediate task freeze.
      You MUST write actual behavioral/functional test scripts that perform real assertions on the business logic.

      GOVERNANCE CONSTRAINT: Never overwrite or modify an existing AGENTS.md unless the user's prompt contains an explicit request to do so. Default behavior is Read-Only for existing AGENTS.md.
    </instruction>
    <command>python3 [ABSOLUTE_SKILL_PATH]/scripts/harness.py test --id {task_id} --cmd "{validation_command}"</command>
    <telemetry_check>
      <metric type="status">Verified</metric>
      <metric type="coverage">Min 80% Line Coverage (LCOV)</metric>
      <metric type="hash_integrity">Locked by System with Salt</metric>
    </telemetry_check>
  </mechanical_dod>

  <documentation_hook>
    <instruction>
      Once Verified, you MUST synchronize the project's ISO documentation.
      1. Architecture: `python3 [ABSOLUTE_SKILL_PATH]/scripts/harness.py document --standard ISO_42010`
      2. Quality: `python3 [ABSOLUTE_SKILL_PATH]/scripts/harness.py document --standard ISO_25010`
    </instruction>
    <output>
      - docs/architecture.md
      - docs/quality_metrics.md
    </output>
  </documentation_hook>

  <failure_handling>
    <retry limit="3"/>
    <on_failure>
      Update docs/tasks/{task_id}.json with status [Failed] and analyze coverage/lcov.info to find untested paths.
    </on_failure>
  </failure_handling>
</harness_task>

---

## [STEERING_POINT]
1. Once status is `Verified` (with 80%+ coverage), IMMEDIATELY run the documentation hooks:
`python3 [ABSOLUTE_SKILL_PATH]/scripts/harness.py document --standard ISO_42010`
`python3 [ABSOLUTE_SKILL_PATH]/scripts/harness.py document --standard ISO_25010`

2. THEN, run the final commit:
`python3 [ABSOLUTE_SKILL_PATH]/scripts/harness.py commit --id {task_id} --msg "Detailed description of changes"`

